  <h2 class="sr-only" id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions About Pet-Friendly Stays at Corbett Foothills Retreat</h2>
  <section class="bg-cfr-green-dark py-16 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="faqs">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-10 space-y-4">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5 transition-all duration-200 open:border-cfr-green-accent">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-sm font-semibold text-cfr-sand-200">
            Are all types of pets welcome at Corbett Foothills Retreat?
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-white/40 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">We primarily welcome dogs, as our property and facilities are best suited for them. We evaluate other types of pets on a case-by-case basis. Please contact us before booking if you are travelling with a pet other than a dog so we can confirm arrangements.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5 transition-all duration-200 open:border-cfr-green-accent">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-sm font-semibold text-cfr-sand-200">
            Do you charge extra for pets?
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-white/40 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">No. We do not charge any extra fees, deposits, or surcharges for pets. Your pet stays as a welcome guest, not a paid add-on. This is part of our commitment to making pet-friendly travel accessible and stress-free.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5 transition-all duration-200 open:border-cfr-green-accent">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-sm font-semibold text-cfr-sand-200">
            Are there any restrictions on where pets can go on the property?
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-white/40 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">Pets are welcome in all outdoor areas, including lawns, gardens, farm areas (on leash near animals), and outdoor dining spaces. They are allowed in guest rooms and common indoor areas. The only restriction is near the forest boundary, where pets must be on a leash at all times for their safety and the safety of local wildlife.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5 transition-all duration-200 open:border-cfr-green-accent">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-sm font-semibold text-cfr-sand-200">
            Can I leave my pet alone in the room?
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-white/40 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">We recommend against leaving pets alone in the room for extended periods, as unfamiliar surroundings may cause anxiety. However, if your pet is comfortable being alone for short durations, please inform us so we can ensure housekeeping schedules and noise levels are coordinated appropriately.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5 transition-all duration-200 open:border-cfr-green-accent">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-sm font-semibold text-cfr-sand-200">
            What should I bring for my pet?
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-white/40 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">Bring your pet's regular food, treats, a portable water bowl, leash, collar with ID tag, waste bags, bedding or blanket for comfort, and any medications. We provide fresh water bowls on request. A familiar toy or chewy can help your pet settle in more comfortably in the new environment.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5 transition-all duration-200 open:border-cfr-green-accent">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-sm font-semibold text-cfr-sand-200">
            Are there any dog-friendly activities and experiences?
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-white/40 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">Yes. Your leashed dog can join you on nature walks, garden tours, and farm visits. The open lawns and grounds are perfect for playtime and exploration. Evening bonfires are pet-friendly as well. Activities that involve entering the forest or safari zones are not suitable for pets due to wildlife safety concerns.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5 transition-all duration-200 open:border-cfr-green-accent">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-sm font-semibold text-cfr-sand-200">
            Is the property safe for small or elderly dogs?
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-white/40 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">Yes, the property is very safe for dogs of all sizes and energy levels. The grounds are enclosed, well-maintained, and free of hazards. There are no steep drops, busy roads, or aggressive animals on the property. Small and elderly dogs can enjoy gentle walks on the lawns without the exertion required by more rugged terrains.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5 transition-all duration-200 open:border-cfr-green-accent">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-sm font-semibold text-cfr-sand-200">
            What if my pet has an emergency during the stay?
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-white/40 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">Ramnagar town, just 8 kilometres away, has veterinary clinics that can handle emergencies. Our team can assist with transport and contact information in case of an urgent situation. We recommend carrying your pet's medical records and your veterinarian's contact number when travelling.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5 transition-all duration-200 open:border-cfr-green-accent">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-sm font-semibold text-cfr-sand-200">
            Can I bring my pet to the farm animal area?
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-white/40 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">Yes, but your pet must be on a leash and under control near the farm animal enclosures. Our resident goats and chickens are accustomed to dogs but may become stressed if approached too enthusiastically. If your dog has a strong prey drive, we recommend observing the farm animals from a respectful distance for everyone's comfort.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

